# Production build only. Vite reads this during `npm run build`, so the live
# site talks to the Laravel API while `npm run dev` keeps running against the
# local data files.
#
# "/" means SAME ORIGIN. The site and the API share one domain: deploy.sh
# copies this build into backend/public and the document root points there, so
# Laravel serves the SPA and /api/* from the same host. Requests go out as
# plain relative paths -- /api/event -- so there is no CORS, no subdomain, and
# no certificate to manage separately.
#
# An absolute origin (https://api.example.com) also works if the API is ever
# split onto its own host. Never put a token here: every VITE_ variable is
# compiled into the public bundle.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/
